# Rule: Scroll animations & cockpit hooks

Shared scroll progress, cockpit integration, and home-v2 corridor-exit compositing. Changes affect Lenis, GSAP, HUD behavior, and the corridor→Services seam.

**Read first:** `sentinel/decisions/002-scroll-animation-architecture.md`, `sentinel/decisions/005-scroll-captured-content-reveal.md`, `sentinel/decisions/018-home-v2-depth-corridor.md`, `sentinel/decisions/021-corridor-exit-zoom-dissipate.md`.

**Process:** `sentinel/MAINTENANCE.md` - document contract changes with an ADR or decision addendum.

**Corridor-exit next station is `#about` (ADR-033).** `useCorridorExitScroll` resolves `nextStation = #about ?? #continuum` — the bio is an ordinary OPAQUE station that IS the cover ending the services ambient hold. The `--tools-bg-in` channel (the retired `#tools` transparent lead-in) is DELETED. `NEXT_STATION_FADE_START_VH = 0.6 / END_VH = 0.0`: the ambient bed + receded mark die exactly as `#about`'s top reaches the viewport top. `#about` carries the veil z-lift + `content-visibility: visible` escape under `data-corridor-exit` (home-v2.css). The Build-park cases terrace adds NO scroll writer — click-owned, gate-only reads; its lateral camera shift is applied in BOTH `FlyingCameraRig` and the DOM mirror camera (ADR-034).

**Home-v2 corridor-exit invariant (ADR-021, 2026-06-19 amendment + follow-up):** the production seam after the corridor epilogue is a **short zoom-dissipate** that resolves as `#services` (now a content section — terminal Keynote/Workshop/Embedded cards mounted via `ServicesPortal`) reaches the viewport top. `useCorridorExitScroll` owns the dissipate clock: `DISSIPATE_SCROLL_SPAN_VH = 0.9` (was 2.0), eased through `corridorExitSpeedRamp` (smootherstep) into `--corridor-dissipate` / `dockProgress`. The hook also writes `data-corridor-docked` (fixed canvas promotion), `data-corridor-exit` + `--corridor-exit-veil` (body veil capped at `VEIL_DOCK_CAP = 0.55` during dock, then lower during ambient). The brandmark fades out with the dissipating sphere across `DISSIPATE_FADE_START 0.5 → DISSIPATE_FADE_END 0.95` of the smoothed dock clock (applied in `ProjectedBrandmarkActor`'s tracker `onPaint` and the post-active rAF) — NO in-section re-centre, hold, or pixel-field. `data-services-ambient` is allowed as a background-only continuation: it keeps the inside-sphere particles/starfield fixed behind Services content for the WHOLE section (released only as `#continuum` approaches, `CONTINUUM_FADE_START_VH 0.5 → 0.1`), without showing the centred SVG or pixel field. The sphere SURFACE is held at a low floor (`SERVICES_AMBIENT_SURFACE_LEVEL` in `ShellSubstrateGyro`, SELECTED continuous like the interior cloud) instead of fading to 0, so the scattered shell reads as a persistent particle bed rather than emptying out at the deepest camera pose; surface visibility/point-size boosts are bridged via `interiorHeld`, and `VEIL_AMBIENT_CAP` (0.3) sits below the dock veil cap so the bed stays visible. The camera pose is unchanged across the dock→ambient seam. Keep the dock channel (`docked` / `dockProgress`) writes scoped to one hook; do not write `epilogueProgress` / `paintProgress` from the exit hook. The retired cover-plane sweep recipe (lower opaque plane covers a held canvas, first-read copy lives inside the cover) is preserved in `components/landing/home-v2/handoff-lab/` + `/test/handoff-a|b|c` and documented in ADR-021 — reuse that recipe verbatim if a later section needs an Active Theory / Hashgraph-class cover sweep; do not rebuild it.

**Retired in-#services brandmark beats (ADR-021 2026-06-19 amendment — do NOT reintroduce without an ADR amendment):** the brandmark-specific choreography phases that once owned `#services` are retired in favour of content plus a background-only ambient layer: (1) **welded re-centre lerp** in `ProjectedBrandmarkActor` (`DOCK_RECENTRE_FRAC` + the welded → viewport-centre lerp + `getServicesTargetHalfPx` local helper); (2) **`data-services-brandmark`** actor-lifecycle gate (`"hold"` / `"fade"`) + `--services-brandmark` opacity var + the continuum-approach fade; (3) **`data-services-pixelate`** + `--services-pixelate` + `transform.seamMorph` + the `CorridorSeamPixelField` 2D canvas mount. `data-services-ambient` / `--services-ambient` / `servicesAmbientLevel` are NOT a brandmark beat anymore; they are the allowed background continuation that keeps `ShellSubstrateGyro` interior cloud + `StaticStarfield` visible behind the cards and keeps `BrandmarkPhysicsCoreActor` hidden (`handoffFade = 0`). The supporting pure helpers (`servicesAmbientOpacityMultiplier`, `SERVICES_AMBIENT_HOLD_LEVEL`, `lib/home-v2/seamPixelize.ts`, `getServicesTargetHalfPx` canonical export) stay in the tree as reusable reference material; the store still carries `seamMorph` / `servicesAmbient` / `servicesAmbientLevel`, with `seamMorph` always inert on the production path. If a future section needs the retired brandmark or pixel recipes, port them verbatim from this ADR's history — do not rebuild from scratch.

**Allowed Services hologram (ADR-025):** the section-owned R3F hologram mounted inside `components/landing/home-v2/services/ServicesStage.tsx` is permitted. It is content for the Services stage, keyed to curated scan notes and service cards, and may publish projected anchors through `hologramConnectorStore`. This does NOT revive the retired fixed viewport `data-services-brandmark` / `data-services-pixelate` choreography above; those attributes and `CorridorSeamPixelField` remain forbidden on the production path.

**Hero → Thoughtform seam invariant (ADR-022 v8):** the hero → corridor seam is a **ToyFight curtain reveal** — the **hero is the moving layer** (`.hero`, `position: relative; z-index: 4`) that scrolls up and off the first viewport, uncovering the corridor's parked `ThoughtformCompassGate` frame held **frozen** behind it (`.home-corridor-host` z:3). NOT the inverse (v7's mistake: a held hero with the corridor rising to cover it), and NEVER a proxy/copy of the second section (v6's mistake). The freeze: `useLandingScroll` toggles `html[data-corridor-entry]` while the corridor stage top is below the viewport top, and `home-v2.css` makes `.home-v2-stage__sticky` `position: fixed; inset: 0` under that flag. At the handoff the flag clears and native sticky resumes at the same `top: 0`, with no transform on the sticky cell and never on `.home-v2-stage`. The hero may receive only a tiny capped inertial `translateY` correction for ToyFight-like smoothness; document scroll, corridor `progress` / `paintProgress` / `epilogueProgress` / `dockProgress`, and the hero video opacity remain untouched. Hero video stays opaque, never scaled/faded (ADR-008 Rule 3, gateway shield). ADR-022 history documents every superseded approach (v6 proxy sweep, v7 held-hero parallax/counter-translate) and its artifact.
